    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Funeral‑etiquette guidelines advise against music that is loud, fast, or overtly celebratory because such music can disrupt the mournful atmosphere.",
      "evidence": "Published etiquette manuals (e.g., \"The Funeral Planner\", \"Funeral Etiquette for Families\") and surveys of funeral directors noting low incidence of high‑energy tracks.",
